 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Index-Based Upsampling with Recalibration](2352-index-based-upsampling-with-recalibration.md)
-Upsamples low-resolution tensors to high resolution using an index map and a recalibration map, specifically for depth values. It gathers values from the low-resolution tensor using the index map. It multiplies the gathered values by the recalibration map to adjust for resolution changes. Choose it when explicit coordinate-based upsampling with recalibration is required for depth data [G].
+Upsamples low-resolution tensors to high resolution by gathering values via an index map and scaling them with a recalibration map, specifically designed for depth values. It differs from sibling methods like Depth-Aware Upsampling by relying on explicit index and scaling tensors rather than depth-weighted interpolation.
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-**Time Complexity:** $O(H' \cdot W')$, where $H'$ and $W'$ are the new dimensions [G].
-**Memory Complexity:** $O(H' \cdot W')$ for the index map and grid map [G].
-**Measured performance:** Not given in the sources [S1, unofficial].
-**Strengths:** Provides explicit coordinate mapping for resolution transformations [S1, unofficial].
-**Limitations:** Requires careful handling of boundary conditions and index validation [G].
-**When to use:** When optimizing shapes from 2D observations using differentiable renderers that require coordinate mapping between resolutions [S1, unofficial].
-**When not to use:** For simple visualization or when standard interpolation is sufficient [G].
+- **Time Complexity:** $O(H_{new} \cdot W_{new})$ for generating the grid map and index map.
+- **Memory Complexity:** $O(H_{new} \cdot W_{new})$ for storing the grid map and index map.
+- **Strengths:** Provides explicit coordinate mappings which can be useful for differentiable rendering or precise upsampling.
+- **Limitations:** The method is specific to the coordinate generation and does not handle value aggregation. The pitfall regarding index bounds requires careful handling of scale factors and grid dimensions.
